Found in k23 review (HEAD 40c7bb3). Only the starter reads CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (bin/briefing:512, for the binary cache). Skills, agents, plugins and settings are read from ~/.claude in lib/App/Briefing.pm and hooks/briefing-preload, so a Claude Code started with CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR resolves user skills and plugins from a different place than briefing searches. Done when resolution follows Claude Code's own rule for that variable (check Claude Code's documented behaviour first), in both implementations, with tests.
